    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0172" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg72"/>

                <head>No. 56.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Putnam.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-09-07"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 7,
                        1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: A note has been received from the chargé
                    d’affaires <hi rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi> of Belgium in this country,
                    conveying an invitation to this government to nominate one or more delegates to
                    attend the international congress of commerce and industry which assembles this
                    month at Brussels. No provision having been made by Congress to meet the
                    invitation by a direct appointment associated with compensation, I have simply
                    to state that you will be and are hereby authorized to take part in the proposed
                    congress (at your own discretion) in sufficient representation of the United
                    States, and to associate with you therein Mr. Wilson, consul at Brussels, should
                    he consent. If preferred, Mr. Wilson can act as the sole delegate.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
